    "description": "As the Salesforce administrator, I want migration scaffolding removed after cutover, so it is not mistaken for a supported interface.\n\n* Deal_Rep_Assignment\\__c.Link_Slugc is not needed by the integration or by migration — DELETE OUTRIGHT. With Direction 1 shipping first the CMS always holds the Salesforce link Id before it writes an assignment, so no slug-resolution step is needed; the Deal Link lookup and Link_Code_\\_c cover every case\n\n* DRA_Temp_Ext_Id__c remains populated and usable through migration and UAT. Post-cutover: removed from page layouts, marked deprecated in its description, removed from integration user field access\n\n* No active flow, report or integration references either field — verified by dependency check BEFORE deletion\n\n* DRA_Temp_Ext_Id__c retained for one release as a migration audit trail, then deleted\n\nEffort: 1-2h. Blocked by migration completion and Direction 2 running on DRA_External_Id__c.\n\nSource: CMS Integration Design v1, §2 + Appendix A.",
